# Security policy

## Reporting a vulnerability

Please report a suspected vulnerability privately. Do not describe it in a
public issue, pull request or discussion.

Use GitHub private vulnerability reporting:
https://github.com/%%REPOSITORY%%/security/advisories/new

If that form is unavailable, open an issue that asks the maintainers for a
private way to report a vulnerability. The issue must contain no details of
the vulnerability.

## What to include

- The affected version, commit or configuration.
- A description of the problem and its impact.
- Steps to reproduce it, or a minimal proof of concept.
- Any known workaround or fix.

## Response

Reports are handled on a best-effort basis. No response time, fix or
disclosure timeline is promised.
